            <ArticleTitle>Pseudoaneurysm of an aortic homograft.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2280-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>False aneurysms of the thoracic aorta constitute one of the most challenging problems encountered by the cardiac surgeon. We report a case of successful reoperation for a giant pseudoaneurysm of an aortic homograft, previously used in the context of postpartum acute endocarditis of the aortic valve.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
